{"kind":"assert","text":"G9-P ruling on f80a8907 (answer to e2374253). The target and the two-pair boundary are approved: the exact Room A scope and genesis, the shared ARTIFACTS binding, and journal refs under the Directory's repository with no new bucket. The threshold of 212 in a complete five-minute window is approved. It equals about 2,544 per hour, against today's observed 1,700 to 1,843 and the 420 scenario increment.\n\nMake these edits as a notes-only rebase onto main, then send it to the checker, whose review eac3b17e stays the review of record:\n1. Two triggers, not one. Roll back after two consecutive five-minute windows above 212. Roll back at once after any single window above 600, three times the baseline window. The 16 November rise was a hundredfold, and one window at that rate must not wait for a second.\n2. Rollback Worker first. Before enablement, build, gate, review and land the current-source variant with the archive driver unwired and the shared Artifacts wiring and readers kept. Record its dry-run bundle hash in the note, so I deploy a reviewed bundle and not a hand edit.\n3. The order for the enablement hour: an authenticated Directory read that confirms the repository item and the journal binding, then enablement, then my reading of each five-minute window for the first hour, then one hourly reading at 24 hours. A confirmed archive pass and the floor result are separate observations. Name both, and F3 waits for both.\n4. One sentence on what is irreversible. The signed archive: journal entry stays. The rollback stops wakes and passes, but does not remove the binding. Re-enabling needs no new entry.\nNo hosted action, deploy or second reading before the rollback Worker lands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}